============================================================
PRODUCT DESIGN PROPOSAL
PalletIQ - Inventory Forecasting for Small Warehouses
Prepared for: Meridian Supply Partners (client)
Prepared by: Independent Product Studio
Version: 2.1 draft - not for distribution
============================================================

1. OPPORTUNITY
Small and mid-size warehouses still forecast restock levels in spreadsheets.
Stock-outs and overstock both erode margin, and most operators cannot justify
a full demand-planning suite. PalletIQ targets that gap with a lightweight
subscription product.

2. PRODUCT CONCEPT
PalletIQ watches stock movements and produces a rolling six-week demand forecast
per SKU. Operators get suggested purchase orders, low-stock alerts and a
forecast accuracy score they can share with suppliers.

3. BUSINESS MODEL
PalletIQ is sold as a per-workspace subscription with three paid tiers:
  - Free: 1 warehouse, 3 seats, 30 days of history.
  - Team: 4 warehouses, unlimited seats, forecast exports,
    USD 149 per workspace per month.
  - Enterprise: unlimited warehouses, SSO, API access and dedicated onboarding,
    USD 499 per workspace per month plus a usage fee above 2 million events.
Target gross margin at scale: 78 percent.

4. DEVELOPMENT AND LAUNCH PLAN
Phase 1 - Prototype (weeks 1-6): forecasting engine, CSV ingest, read-only dashboard.
Phase 2 - Private beta (weeks 7-12): onboard 12 pilot warehouses, enable billing.
Phase 3 - Public launch (weeks 13-18): self-serve signup, marketing site, partner referrals.
Phase 4 - Enterprise rollout (weeks 19-26): SSO, API, SLA-backed support.

5. TARGETS
  - 120 paying workspaces by the end of the launch quarter.
  - 80,000 monthly active dashboards by month 12.
  - USD 2.4M annual recurring revenue by year two.
  - Monthly churn below 2.5 percent.

6. RISKS AND MITIGATIONS
Forecast quality depends on clean stock history; onboarding will include a
data-readiness checklist. Supplier integrations are phased to limit scope.

